Third-party notices
-------------------
The full list — every npm package in the web bundle with its version, license and license text, the fonts Excalidraw
bundles, and the Korean font subsets — is in THIRD_PARTY_NOTICES.md (generated by packaging/notices.py from
web/package-lock.json; it also ships inside the web bundle). Main components:
  - Excalidraw (@excalidraw/excalidraw) — MIT; its bundled fonts (dist/fonts: Excalifont, Virgil, Xiaolai, Nunito,
    Lilita One, Assistant, Cascadia Code — SIL OFL 1.1; Comic Shanns — MIT; Liberation Sans 1.05 — GPL-2.0 with
    font exception)
  - React, React DOM — MIT
  - MathJax (mathjax-full) — Apache-2.0
  - Other bundled npm packages under MIT, ISC, BSD-3-Clause, Apache-2.0, (MPL-2.0 OR Apache-2.0), (MIT AND Zlib),
    Unlicense, 0BSD and CC0-1.0 — see THIRD_PARTY_NOTICES.md
  - Korean font subsets — Gaegu, Noto Sans KR, Nanum Pen Script, Black Han Sans, Nanum Gothic Coding, Jua,
    Nanum Myeongjo, Dokdo, Poor Story, Do Hyeon — SIL Open Font License 1.1 (see web/public/kfonts/LICENSE.txt)

Code ported into this repository:
  - server/fracindex.py — ported from rocicorp/fractional-indexing 3.2.0 (src/index.js),
    https://github.com/rocicorp/fractional-indexing — CC0-1.0 (public domain dedication, no rights reserved).

Ideas only (no code copied):
  - excalidraw-mcp and mcp_excalidraw (MIT) — the shape of an MCP server that draws Excalidraw elements.
